msgid ""
"This FAQ has undergone countless revisions and improvements by a diverse "
"group of contributors over the past decades."
msgstr "在过去几十年里，这份常见问题解答经过了众多贡献者无数次修订和改进。"

#, no-wrap
#~ msgid "Frequently Asked Questions, and answers, covering all aspects of FreeBSD"
#~ msgstr "FreeBSD 方方面面的常见问题和回答"

#, no-wrap
#~ msgid "Frequently Asked Questions for FreeBSD {rel2-relx} and {rel-relx}"
#~ msgstr "FreeBSD {rel2-relx} 与 {rel-relx} 的常见问题"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The latest version of this document is always available from the extref:"
#~ "{faq}[FreeBSD website].  It may also be downloaded as one large link:."
#~ "[HTML] file with HTTP or as a variety of other formats from the https://"
#~ "download.freebsd.org/doc/[FreeBSD FTP server]."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "该文档的最新版本可随时在 extref:{faq}[FreeBSD 官网] 上查阅。你可以通过 "
#~ "HTTP 下载单个大 link:.[HTML] 文件，也可以在 https://download.freebsd.org/"
#~ "doc/[FreeBSD FTP server] 上下载众多其他格式的文档。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "FreeBSD is a modern operating system for desktops, laptops, servers, and "
#~ "embedded systems with support for a large number of https://www.FreeBSD."
#~ "org/platforms/[platforms]."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "FreeBSD 是一套可用于台式电脑、笔记本电脑、服务器及嵌入式系统，且支持大量 "
#~ "https://www.FreeBSD.org/platforms/[平台] 的现代操作系统。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "It is based on U.C. Berkeley's \"4.4BSD-Lite\" release, with some "
#~ "\"4.4BSD-Lite2\" enhancements.  It is also based indirectly on William "
#~ "Jolitz's port of U.C. Berkeley's \"Net/2\" to the i386(TM), known as "
#~ "\"386BSD\", though very little of the 386BSD code remains."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "该系统基于加利福尼亚大学伯克利分校 (U.C. Berkeley) 发布的 \"4.4BSD-Lite"
#~ "\"，并带有 \"4.4BSD-Lite2\" 的一些改进。该系统还间接基于 William Jolitz 编"
#~ "写的伯克利分校 \"Net/2\" 的 i386™ 移植版本，通常称为 \"386BSD\"，然而仅极"
#~ "少部分的 386BSD 代码留存在 FreeBSD 中。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "FreeBSD is used by companies, Internet Service Providers, researchers, "
#~ "computer professionals, students and home users all over the world in "
#~ "their work, education and recreation."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "FreeBSD 用于世界各地的公司、互联网运营商 (ISP)、研究人员、计算机专业人员、"
#~ "学生及家用用户在他们的工作、教育和生产中。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "For more detailed information on FreeBSD, refer to the extref:{handbook}"
#~ "[FreeBSD Handbook]."
#~ msgstr "关于 FreeBSD 的更多信息，请参阅 extref:{handbook}[FreeBSD 手册]。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The goal of the FreeBSD Project is to provide a stable and fast general "
#~ "purpose operating system that may be used for any purpose without strings "
#~ "attached."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "FreeBSD 项目的目标是提供一个稳定、快速并可用于任何用途的通用操作系统，不附"
#~ "加任何额外条件。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Yes.  Those restrictions do not control how the code is used, but how to "
#~ "treat the FreeBSD Project itself.  The license itself is available at "
#~ "https://www.FreeBSD.org/copyright/freebsd-license/[license] and can be "
#~ "summarized like this:"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "有的。这些限制不规定如何使用代码，而是规定如何对待 FreeBSD 项目本身。许可"
#~ "证的详细内容可参阅 https://www.FreeBSD.org/copyright/freebsd-license/"
#~ "[FreeBSD 许可证] ，主要内容可概括为："

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Many of us have a significant investment in the project and would "
#~ "certainly not mind a little financial compensation now and then, but we "
#~ "definitely do not insist on it.  We believe that our first and foremost "
#~ "\"mission\" is to provide code to any and all comers, and for whatever "
#~ "purpose, so that the code gets the widest possible use and provides the "
#~ "widest possible benefit.  This, we believe, is one of the most "
#~ "fundamental goals of Free Software and one that we enthusiastically "
#~ "support."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "我们中的很多人对此项目做出了巨大的贡献，对一些经济补偿当然不会推辞，但我们"
#~ "绝对不会依赖于此。我们认为，我们的首要“使命”是对一切用户提供项目代码，不论"
#~ "他们出于何种目的。这样项目代码就能尽可能被广泛使用，让尽可能多的人受益。我"
#~ "们认为这是自由软件最基本的目标之一，而且这也是我们尽全力支持的。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Most people do not actually use an operating system.  They use "
#~ "applications.  The applications are what really use the operating "
#~ "system.  FreeBSD is designed to provide a robust and full-featured "
#~ "environment for applications.  It supports a wide variety of web "
#~ "browsers, office suites, email readers, graphics programs, programming "
#~ "environments, network servers, and much more.  Most of these applications "
#~ "can be managed through the https://www.FreeBSD.org/ports/[Ports "
#~ "Collection]."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "许多人使用的其实不是操作系统，而是应用程序。那些应用程序才真正使用操作系"
#~ "统。FreeBSD 为给应用程序提供可靠且全功能的环境而设计。FreeBSD 支持大量的网"
#~ "页浏览器、办公套件、邮件阅读器、图形程序、编程环境、网络服务器等等众多软"
#~ "件。其中多数软件可以通过 https://www.FreeBSD.org/ports/[移植软件集 (Ports "
#~ "Collection)] 管理。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "If an application is only available on one operating system, that "
#~ "operating system cannot just be replaced.  Chances are, there is a very "
#~ "similar application on FreeBSD, however.  As a solid office or Internet "
#~ "server or a reliable workstation, FreeBSD will almost certainly do "
#~ "everything you need.  Many computer users across the world, including "
#~ "both novices and experienced UNIX(R) administrators, use FreeBSD as their "
#~ "only desktop operating system."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "如果一个应用程序只能安装在一种操作系统上，那么你不能替换这个操作系统。但"
#~ "是，FreeBSD 上会有非常相似的应用程序。无论是作为固定的办公电脑、网络服务器"
#~ "还是可靠的工作站，FreeBSD 都可以做你任何想做的事情。世界各地的许多计算机用"
#~ "户，包括新手和经验丰富的 UNIX® 管理员，都将 FreeBSD 作为他们的唯一桌面操作"
#~ "系统使用。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Users migrating to FreeBSD from another UNIX(R)-like environment will "
#~ "find FreeBSD to be similar.  Windows(R) and Mac OS(R) users may be "
#~ "interested in instead using https://www.ghostbsd.org/[GhostBSD], https://"
#~ "www.midnightbsd.org/[MidnightBSD] or https://www.nomadbsd.org/[NomadBSD] "
#~ "three FreeBSD-based desktop distributions.  Non-UNIX(R) users should "
#~ "expect to invest some additional time learning the UNIX(R) way of doing "
#~ "things.  This FAQ and the extref:{handbook}[FreeBSD Handbook] are "
#~ "excellent places to start."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "之前使用其他类 UNIX(R) 环境，后来转移到 FreeBSD 的用户将会以他们熟悉的方式"
#~ "使用 FreeBSD。Windows(R) 和 Mac OS(R) 用户可能对 https://www.ghostbsd.org/"
#~ "[GhostBSD], https://www.midnightbsd.org/[MidnightBSD] 或 https://www."
#~ "nomadbsd.org/[NomadBSD] 这三个基于 FreeBSD 的桌面发行版更感兴趣。非 "
#~ "UNIX(R) 用户可能需要花些时间学习 UNIX(R) 下做事的方式。这个常见问题集和 "
#~ "extref:{handbook}[FreeBSD 手册] 是开始学习这些知识的好地方。"

#~ msgid "It may be used free of charge, even by commercial users."
#~ msgstr "对包括商业用户在内的任何用户而言，它可以免费 (free) 使用。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Full source for the operating system is freely available, and the minimum "
#~ "possible restrictions have been placed upon its use, distribution and "
#~ "incorporation into other work (commercial or non-commercial)."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "该操作系统的所有源代码都可以免费且自由地 (freely) 获取，对源代码的使用、分"
#~ "发及（商业或非商业地）合并在其他工作中的限制在可能的范围内尽可能少。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Anyone who has an improvement or bug fix is free to submit their code and "
#~ "have it added to the source tree (subject to one or two obvious "
#~ "provisions)."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "任何想要改进 FreeBSD 和修复其 bug 的人都可以自由地提交代码并将其加入代码树"
#~ "（需要遵守一两条明确的规定）。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "James Howard wrote a good explanation of the history and differences "
#~ "between the various projects, called https://jameshoward.us/archive/bsd-"
#~ "family-tree/[The BSD Family Tree] which goes a fair way to answering this "
#~ "question.  Some of the information is out of date, but the history "
#~ "portion in particular remains accurate."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "James Howard 写了一篇文章 https://jameshoward.us/archive/bsd-family-tree/"
#~ "[《BSD 家族》(The BSD Family Tree)] ，里面很好地解释了这些项目的历史和区"
#~ "别，公正地回答了这个问题。一些信息可能已经过时，但是有关历史的部分仍是准确"
#~ "的。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Most of the BSDs share patches and code, even today.  All of the BSDs "
#~ "have common ancestry."
#~ msgstr "多数 BSD 系统至今还在共享补丁和代码。这些 BSD 系统有着共同的祖先。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The design goals of FreeBSD are described in <<FreeBSD-goals>>, above.  "
#~ "The design goals of the other most popular BSDs may be summarized as "
#~ "follows:"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "FreeBSD 的设计目标在上面的 <<FreeBSD-goals>> 一节已经解释了。其他常见 BSD "
#~ "系统的设计目标可以总结如下："

#~ msgid ""
#~ "OpenBSD aims for operating system security above all else.  The OpenBSD "
#~ "team wrote man:ssh[1] and man:pf[4], which have both been ported to "
#~ "FreeBSD."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "OpenBSD 致力于设计比其他系统更安全 (security) 的操作系统。OpenBSD 团队编写"
#~ "了 man:ssh[1] 和 man:pf[4]，这些软件已被移植到 FreeBSD 中。"

#~ msgid "NetBSD aims to be easily ported to other hardware platforms."
#~ msgstr "NetBSD 致力于设计易于在各硬件平台中移植的操作系统。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "DragonFly BSD is a fork of FreeBSD 4.8 that has since developed many "
#~ "interesting features of its own, including the HAMMER file system and "
#~ "support for user-mode \"vkernels\"."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "DragonFly BSD 是 FreeBSD 4.8 的一个分支，开发了许多自己有意思的功能，比如 "
#~ "HAMMER 文件系统和用户模式的 \"vkernels\"。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "At any point in the development of FreeBSD, there can be multiple "
#~ "parallel branches.  {rel-relx} releases are made from the {rel-stable} "
#~ "branch, and {rel2-relx} releases are made from the {rel2-stable} branch."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "在 FreeBSD 开发过程的任何节点处，都可能有多条平行分支。{rel-relx} 基于 "
#~ "{rel-stable} 分支开发，{rel2-relx} 基于 {rel2-stable} 开发。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Up until the release of 12.0, the {rel2-relx} series was the one known as "
#~ "_-STABLE_.  However, as of {rel-head-relx}, the {rel2-relx} branch will "
#~ "be designated for an \"extended support\" status and receive only fixes "
#~ "for major problems, such as security-related fixes."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "直到 12.0 版本发布之时，{rel2-relx} 系列被称作 _-STABLE_ 版。然而，当 "
#~ "{rel-head-relx} 发布时，{rel2-relx} 将进入“扩展支持”状态，仅修复关键问题，"
#~ "比如安全相关的问题。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "More information on FreeBSD releases can be found on the https://www."
#~ "FreeBSD.org/releng/#release-build[Release Engineering page] and in man:"
#~ "release[7]."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "关于 FreeBSD 公开版本的更多信息，请参阅 https://www.FreeBSD.org/releng/"
#~ "#release-build[发布工程页] 和 man:release[7] 。"

#, no-wrap
#~ msgid "What is _FreeBSD-CURRENT_?"
#~ msgstr "什么是 _FreeBSD-CURRENT_ ？"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "extref:{handbook}cutting-edge/[FreeBSD-CURRENT, current] is the "
#~ "development version of the operating system, which will in due course "
#~ "become the new FreeBSD-STABLE branch.  As such, it is really only of "
#~ "interest to developers working on the system and die-hard hobbyists.  See "
#~ "the extref:{handbook}cutting-edge/[relevant section, current] in the "
#~ "extref:{handbook}[Handbook] for details on running _-CURRENT_."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "extref:{handbook}cutting-edge/[FreeBSD-CURRENT, current] 是 FreeBSD 的开发"
#~ "版本，将在某个时期转变为新的 FreeBSD-STABLE 分支。因此，该分支仅适合对开发"
#~ "该系统感兴趣的开发者以及非常硬核的爱好者。 关于运行 _-CURRENT_ 版本的更多"
#~ "信息，请参阅 extref:{handbook}[手册] 中的 extref:{handbook}cutting-edge/"
#~ "[有关章节, current] 。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Users not familiar with FreeBSD should not use FreeBSD-CURRENT.  This "
#~ "branch sometimes evolves quite quickly and due to mistakes can be un-"
#~ "buildable at times.  People that use FreeBSD-CURRENT are expected to be "
#~ "able to analyze, debug, and report problems."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "不熟悉 FreeBSD 的用户不应当使用 FreeBSD-CURRENT。这个分支有时演化得很快，"
#~ "由于时而产生的问题可能造成分支无法构建。使用 FreeBSD-CURRENT 的用户应该可"
#~ "以分析、调试和反馈问题。"

